Design the shared pieces. A private final class near `_WalkResult`:

```dart
/// Per-step walk state shared by the incremental [_walk] and the full
/// [_rebuild] pass: the pending-table boundary-latch bookkeeping (gh-1573)
/// lives in exactly ONE place — a drift between the two loops would
/// desynchronize the commit boundary between the incremental and rebuild
/// paths.
final class _TableWalkState {
  _TableWalkState();

  /// Outputs per consumed source line.
  final List<List<String>> outsPerLine = [];
  final List<bool> fenceAfter = [];
  /// Whether the pending-table buffer was NON-EMPTY just BEFORE each
  /// consumed line (see [_WalkResult.tableBefore]).
  final List<bool> tableBefore = [];
  /// Absolute src index where the pending span began, per consumed line
  /// (see [_WalkResult.pendingStartAt]).
  final List<int> pendingStartAt = [];

  /// Absolute src index where the in-flight pending span began (-1 when
  /// none is open). A seeded walk starts inside (or at the head of) an
  /// already-open span: the seed occupies src[from-seed.length..from).
  int pendingStart = -1;

  /// Last step whose completion left no pending table (-1 = none yet).
  int lastClean = -1;

  /// Fence state after [lastClean].
  bool fenceAtClean = false;
}
```

And the step function — where? A method on TranscriptMarkdown (needs no fields) or a top-level function taking fmt. Since both loops call it with different formatters, make it a private top-level function or a static method. As a method on TranscriptMarkdown taking the formatter as a parameter is also fine. I'll do a top-level private function right after `_TableWalkState`:

```dart
/// Consumes one source line into [s] through [fmt] — the per-step
/// pending-table bookkeeping (boundary latch) shared by the incremental
/// and rebuild walks. [i] is the absolute src index of [line].
void _tableWalkStep(AnsiMarkdown fmt, String line, int i, _TableWalkState s) {
  if (fmt.hasPendingTable && s.pendingStart < 0) s.pendingStart = i;
