The redundant `await env.writeFile(_globalConfig, _validGlobal);` (through the outer `env`, cwd `/work`) is deleted from the `cwd == home` test. The test now builds `homeEnv` / `homeService` first and writes the global file only through `homeEnv` — exactly the shape suggested:

```dart
final homeEnv = MemoryExecutionEnv(cwd: '/home');
final homeService = ConfigService(env: homeEnv, homeDir: '/home');
await homeEnv.writeFile(_globalConfig, _validGlobal);
final report = await checkOrThrow(homeService);
```

`cwd == home` test green after the removal (all 77 tests in `config_service_test.dart` pass, including the two new trailing-slash cases).
